# Short memory: bit 0 of the RAM UI5 ($0C00-$0FFF, the low nibble) reads 1 in every word. Commodore's start-up sizes the RAM by writing each byte from $0400 and reading it back: it stops at $0C00, so BASIC gets 2 KB. (Stuck at 0 instead, the bit would pass its test values and the fault would hide.)
machine bw2001
title "Short memory"
brief "The BW-2001 starts and BASIC works, but the banner says 2047 BYTES FREE instead of 7167."
fault column UI5.IO1 1
